# Page — the outermost wrapper of a routed screen: a readable measure, centred,
# with air at the edges. `PageNarrow` is the same thing at prose width, for a
# screen that is one column of reading (an article, a settings form, a sign-up)
# rather than a layout.
#
#     use Page():
#         use Section("Settings", ""):
#             use Form(save):
#                 ...
#
# The width comes from `--fa-maxwidth`, the theme's own token, so an app states
# its page width once — in its `theme:` block — and every page in it agrees. This
# component does not take a width parameter for the same reason `Spacer` does not
# take a pixel count: a container that can be any width is a container that will
# be four slightly different widths.
#
# The rules live in vocabulary.fct, not here. This file is the wrapper; that file
# is the substrate, and a host that wants the measure without the wrapper (inside
# a `for` body, say) applies `.x-l-page` to a box of its own and gets exactly the
# same page.
import "vocabulary.fct"
app FacetLayout:
    component Page():
        box class "x-l-page":
            slot
    component PageNarrow():
        box class "x-l-page x-l-narrow":
            slot
